Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:35:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] fix(ha-vendor): bounded token retry and a distinct
 terminal ID

For running alongside Home Assistant's own vesync integration:
- On a rejected token, log in (at most once per 300 s) and retry the request
  once with the new token, account ID and a fresh traceId in the body and the
  original headers. Never recurse (webdjoe/pyvesync#558).
- Salt TERMINAL_ID so this copy never shares a terminal ID with stock pyvesync
  on the same host.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
